WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.503
-You may know our next guest
from his work on "SNL"

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.071
and "Late Night
with Conan O'Brien,"

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.306
as the creator of characters
like the Chicago Superfans,

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:08.607
The Ambiguously Gay Duo,

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:11.077
and Triumph
the Insult Comic Dog.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:14.113
He co-wrote and co-directed
the hit animated movie "Leo,"

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:16.582
which is streaming now
on Netflix. Let's take a look.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:19.252
-I'm sorry.
-Oh, no, no. Don't be sorry.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:21.521
Just stop. I can't handle it.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.856
-But my mom says
it's good to cry.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:27.260
-Not where I come from.
Here. Let me calm you down.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.896
I'll sing you a lullaby,
and you'll go to sleep.

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:33.799
♪ Don't cry ♪

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:36.869
♪ Crying's for weaklings ♪

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:39.706
♪ Don't cry ♪

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:43.142
♪ It's lazy and dumb ♪

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:45.678
♪ Dry those tears ♪

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.981
♪ They make you look ugly ♪

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.517
♪ Suck it up ♪

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.520
♪ You mustn't succumb ♪

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.355
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.925
our friend Robert Smigel!

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:00.693
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:15.374 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:18.711
-So happy you're here.
-I'm -- It's great to be here.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.880
-That was such a funny clip.
Congratulations.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.382
This is your animated-movie
directing debut.

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:26.486
-This is my animated movie...
Whatever he said.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.321
-All everything I said was true.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:31.190
-Everything. Not a -- Yes.
And I go, you know --

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:34.527
You know, my history is
with sketch comedy right here

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.129
in late-night television.
-Yeah.

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:40.200
-I was, um --
I was the original head writer

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.435
of the Conan iteration
of this show.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:45.438
-Yes, absolutely.
-Back in 19...

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:48.174
Too old. Too old.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.842
And I did want
to congratulate you.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.744
Your show is great.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.579
Means a lot coming from you.
-Writing is great.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.481
Eh. I don't know about that.
But...

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:58.651
But, no, thank you.
The writers are great.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.219
And I wanted
to congratulate them

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.655
not only on getting
another Emmy nomination,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:07.159
but also on continuing
the late-night tradition

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:10.396
of losing to the same guy
for many, many years in a row.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.598
-Yeah.
-Way to go.

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:13.165
-Yeah. Thank you. Same guy.

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:15.634
-Same guy. Oh, well, no, we --
It was Jon Stewart when --

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.169
-You lost to Jon Stewart.

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:18.872
And I am honored
and flattered to lose

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.539
to my friend John Oliver.
-John Oliver.

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:23.109
A great man, but, you know...

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.177
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:28.248
No, I don't know. I mean,
it's a lot. It's a lot of years.

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.515
It's a lot of years to lose.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:31.950
And I was thinking --

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.920
I was thinking,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.156
is there any way you could maybe
get Trump involved, you know,

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:39.525
so he could go all birther
on John Oliver?

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.126
-Oh!
-See what I'm saying?

00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:42.629
-Right. 'Cause he's not --
he wasn't born here.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:43.829
-Yeah.

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:47.366
[as Pres. Trump]
"That's right, folks!

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:52.038
John Oliver has no business
hosting a show!

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:55.441
The 14th Amendment
clearly states

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:58.778
no foreign man...

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.147
shall host a late-night program!

00:03:02.147 --> 00:03:03.749
When I was president,

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:08.020
I got rid of Greg Ferguson,
folks, the same way."

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.889
[Normal voice]
I don't know.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.257
-Very good.
-That's Donald Trump.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.592
Just something to think about.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.727
-It's fun to think about.
-Something to think about.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:17.196
You've had --
It's sort of a boom time,

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.932
not just for you
as a writer or director.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.967
You're also --
A lot of acting roles.

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:23.336
You're actually flying off to
Sundance right now for a film.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.271
-I'm going to Sundance
right after this.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.972
This is so strange.

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:30.443
I'm in a Sundance, like,
competition film.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:32.578
-That's very exciting.
-Yeah, it is very exciting.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:35.414
It's called "Between the
Temples" with Jason Schwartzman.

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:37.183
-Yeah.
-What do you play?

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.884
-Take a guess.

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:42.155
-Okay. Looks like you are --
You are a rabbi.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.589
Yeah. Okay.

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:44.923
-Very good.
-Thank you.

00:03:44.923 --> 00:03:46.859
-I am a rabbi. And now...

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.661
But I've been on, like,
four things this year.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.762
This is...

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:50.863
-So, this is "Burying Bubby."

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.765
-Short film called
"Burying Bubby."

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.500
And what do you think
I'm playing in it?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:59.138
-Looks like a rabbi again.
-Yes, that's a rabbi. Yeah.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.040
But it's a little bit
of a stretch.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.208
It's -- That was --
That guy is a reformed rabbi.

00:04:03.208 --> 00:04:05.077
And the other one,
it's a conservative...

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:07.513
-You got range.
-I definitely have range.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.482
-You were in "What We Do
in the Shadows,"
a fantastic show.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.050
-I love "What We Do
in the Shadows."

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.952
It's an amazing show.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.086
-And there I am with --

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:16.623
This is Nandor.
I love this character.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:20.193
And I played
Nandor's Jewish friend.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.727
-Okay.
-That's literally --

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:24.163
He calls me Alexander the Jew.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.565
-Okay.
-In the show.

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:27.767
-And then "White House
Plumbers," which is a HBO show.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.636
-It's a prestigious
HBO production.

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:32.738
I'm there with --
That's Justin Theroux.

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:35.408
And Woody Harrelson
is in the scene.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.643
He plays Gordon Liddy
from the Watergate.

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:42.515
And I play a prison inmate
who wants a kosher meal.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.483
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:45.718
-Obviously, one of the voices

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.320
you're most known for
is triumph.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.189
-Triumph the Insult Comic Dog.
-Yes.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.958
-Yes.
-Started at

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.793
the Conan O'Brien show.
-Started...

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:56.862
And you were recently at the
Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:04:56.862 --> 00:04:59.531
-Yes.
-So, here, of course,

00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:01.200
we know Triumph, and here is --

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.002
There was a Leo balloon,
which is very exciting.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.470
That was why you were there.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.839
-They actually made
a balloon for Leo.

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:09.976
And so I'm there --
And, um, I don't know.

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:13.446
I just -- It's the corniest show
left on television. I love it.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:16.115
-Oh, Macy's Thanksgiving Day
Parade. The best.

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.384
-Everybody's lip syncing,
and Hoda Kotb

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.519
is reading from a prompter.

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.288
The corniest stuff.

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:24.223
And I'm like,
"I got to bring Triumph.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.192
I know I'm here for Leo, but..."

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:28.827
So I bring the puppet,
and I'm with my son.

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:31.831
-So you didn't -- They didn't
ask you to bring Triumph.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.365
You just had it on your hand.

00:05:33.365 --> 00:05:36.635
-Yeah. Hoda Kotb --

00:05:36.635 --> 00:05:40.473
Hoda Kotb is like,
"What is this show missing?

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:43.375
How about a rubber puppet
to [bleep] on all of us?

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:45.378
That's what we need here."
No.

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:47.780
So I'm, like, having --
I'm taping myself,

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.448
you know, mocking the show.

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:52.251
And then the cast of "Shucked"
comes out.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:53.952
-Yeah.
-A great show.

00:05:53.952 --> 00:05:56.389
And they're lip syncing
like every show does.

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:59.192
It's fantastic. And then
this amazing performer --

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.826
I think we have a clip.
Alex Newell.

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:03.362
-Yeah. absolutely.
So you notice...

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.597
-I notice that she's like
three feet away from me.

00:06:05.597 --> 00:06:07.866
So out comes the puppet.

00:06:07.866 --> 00:06:09.769
-Yeah.
I love this clip

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:12.805
because we realize
you realize you're on TV

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:16.308
and then you realize that means
Triumph can also be on TV.

00:06:16.308 --> 00:06:17.710
Let's take a look.
-Exactly. Yeah.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:22.048
-♪ I'm independently owned
and operated ♪

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:25.818
♪ And every man that I meet
is just intimidated ♪

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:28.554
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.656
-It's like second nature.
-It's second nature.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:33.092
Triumph just got into it.
He started dancing.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.328
I mean, Triumph
is NBC property,

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:37.062
so I figured
there's no legal issue.

00:06:37.062 --> 00:06:39.632
-He is not, however,
CNN property.

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:42.467
And this was, uh -- this was
at a convention years ago.

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:45.170
-Covered the Republican
convention in 2016 for Hulu.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:48.341
-And there's Jake Tapper,
and behind him we see Triumph.

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:50.977
Now, I will say
he's promoting NBC talent.

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:52.311
-I'm loyal.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:53.912
-"We love Matt,
Savannah, and Al."

00:06:53.912 --> 00:06:56.649
Uh, and then here he is again.
What does that say?

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:58.050
"Positive..."

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.886
-"Positively no photobombing."

00:07:00.886 --> 00:07:03.055
He's holding up a sign.
Oh.

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:06.124
And then -- Oh, do you have the
clip of my favorite photobomb?

00:07:06.124 --> 00:07:09.829
It's from, uh, the 2008 --
Do we have that one?

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:11.730
-Yeah. This is, uh --
This is you and Mr. Met.

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:13.298
Triumph, I should say,
and Mr. Met.

00:07:13.298 --> 00:07:14.967
Alright.
-So this is on Fox News.

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:17.235
Go ahead. Roll it.
-Let's take a look.

00:07:17.235 --> 00:07:18.671
-Uh, it's on Fox News.

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:21.206
And I realized
that I can hump Mr. Met

00:07:21.206 --> 00:07:24.243
behind Greta Van Susteren
on Fox News.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:26.479
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:30.549
-Anyway, "Leo"
is a heartwarming story

00:07:30.549 --> 00:07:34.319
of a lizard who finds
the true meaning of his life

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:36.255
is helping children.

00:07:36.255 --> 00:07:37.590
It's for the whole family.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.425
-You also --
There's a Triumph album.

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:40.959
"Come Poop with Me."

00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:42.895
Oh, well, yeah. Well --
So I write songs for "Leo."

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:45.864
I wrote a lot of songs for
"Leo." Uh, but this is --

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:49.067
I wrote "Christmastime
for the Jews" on "SNL,"

00:07:49.067 --> 00:07:51.069
And, uh, yeah,
"Come Poop with Me"

00:07:51.069 --> 00:07:54.006
was, like, the last time I'd
really written a bunch of songs.

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:56.675
Um, you know,
they were quite different.

00:07:56.675 --> 00:07:59.678
I think the most popular one
was "Underage Bichon."

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:01.814
-Yeah.
-Anybody? Anybody?

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.282
"Underage Bichon"?
It was about...

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.683
-Not a lot -- Yeah.

00:08:04.683 --> 00:08:07.353
-...a regrettable incident
in Triumph's, uh, young life.

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:13.325
He had sex with a Poodle that
he thought was a year old...

00:08:13.325 --> 00:08:16.962
but turned out to be
10 months old.

00:08:16.962 --> 00:08:18.797
But he was brave enough
to sing about it.

00:08:18.797 --> 00:08:21.033
-[ Laughs ]
-But this is --

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:24.503
You know, it's -- I'm excited
about "Leo" and the songs.

00:08:24.503 --> 00:08:27.273
-Is any one Oscar-worthy
on "Leo," do you think?

00:08:27.273 --> 00:08:28.674
-Oh, all of them.
-Okay. That's so nice.

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.442
-All of them are. But none
of them are going to win.

00:08:30.442 --> 00:08:31.710
There's, like, a huge --

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.479
I mean, there's like
10 songs from "Barbie."

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:35.147
-That's true.
-That's first in line.

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.483
And then -- I don't know
if you heard about this,

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:39.885
but, um, John Oliver
submitted a song.

00:08:39.885 --> 00:08:42.221
-Oh, well.
-Yeah. It's not even --

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:44.022
-You've got no chance.
-It's not even in a movie!

00:08:44.022 --> 00:08:47.693
-They're just like,
"Right this way, Mr. Oliver."

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:49.995
-You, uh --
One more thing to plug.

00:08:49.995 --> 00:08:51.831
You're doing a show
in San Francisco.

00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:54.399
-Yes, I'm doing
Triumph's game show called

00:08:54.399 --> 00:08:55.567
"Let's Make a Poop."

00:08:55.567 --> 00:08:57.336
-Sure.
-Very exciting.

00:08:57.336 --> 00:09:01.507
Triumph asks questions --
trivia questions to celebrities,

00:09:01.507 --> 00:09:03.509
and they have to answer
with a funny answer.

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:05.611
-That's really good.
-You want to try one?

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:06.878
-Yeah.

00:09:06.878 --> 00:09:09.081
-Okay. So I'll do it
in Triumph's voice here.

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:10.449
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:12.985
[as Triumph] "Donald Trump
calls these people hostages,

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:15.821
but they're more commonly
referred to as is."

00:09:15.821 --> 00:09:17.857
"Who are Melania and Barron?"

00:09:17.857 --> 00:09:19.992
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:21.293
-They're not gonna compete
with Triumph.

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:23.829
[Normal voice] Sunday night
at the Castro Theatre.

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:24.996
-Robert Smigel!

00:09:24.996 --> 00:09:26.265
Tickets for "Let's Make a Poop"

00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:28.901
are available at
sfsketchfest.com!

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:31.203
"Leo" streaming on Netflix.
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

